   "story": "Ridgeline crushed gravel for every road in the valley. When the Cordon closed the roads the crew had nothing to do but sit in the scale house and listen to the radio. The Cordon came for the powder magazine on the fourth day; Pete Haralson, the blaster, wouldn't hand it over without the manager's signature, and the manager had gone home sick. Pete locked himself in with the stick and the caps and the manager's key stayed in the desk drawer where it always was.",
